# Current work (update this file)

**Last updated:** 2026-08-21

## Latest

- Onboard New Employee form fields share one control style (height, border, bg, labels, select chevrons). Department / Designation / Role all use select + `+ Add`; disabled fields use opacity instead of a different background.
- Add Employee catalog fields (Department / Designation / Role): `+ Add` button beside the select (not “+ Add new…” inside the dropdown).
- Regenerated `database/trackerpro-full.sql` from live Postgres (`trackerpro`) via pg_dump — includes `clients."CustomerSince"` and `sub_ventures."Notes"`.
- Customer detail Notes: always under Customer Information; scoped per sub-venture; Notes + All Projects cards share height — only the projects table scrolls. Sub-venture `Notes` column + create/add-client save notes onto that SV.
- Customer All Projects table: fixed columns — Project (name + ID + dates), Health, Stage, Sub-venture, Progress, PM, Open.
- Project details UI polish (Apple HIG): richer header (health/status, timeline, budget, progress), quieter stage band, underline tabs, soft segmented filters (Health/Team/Comm), Tasks search.
- Customer cards follow Apple HIG clarity/deference: identity first, EM as secondary row, unified metrics strip; soft lift on hover.
- Customer detail: At Risk removed from Customer Information; Health filter (All / Healthy / At Risk / Critical) on All Projects top-right.
- Customer project counts are mutually exclusive: **New** (ongoing 0%), **Ongoing**, **Completed** (delivered), **On Hold**, **Archived** (payment done). **Total** = sum of those five. Same breakdown on Customers list cards/table. Shared helper: `lib/client-project-counts.ts`.
- **Customer Since** stored on `clients."CustomerSince"` (date). Set to today (IST) on create; existing rows backfilled from `CreatedAtUtc`. Shown in Customer Information on the detail page (no longer derived from project dates).
- Customer details **Change EM** opens a centered modal (no longer clipped by the header). Loads all employees with designation Engagement Manager from the DB; search filters by name/email/code.
- Customer details **Change EM**: lists employees with designation Engagement Manager (`mst_designations` → `employees`). Shows current EM from `clients`; save updates `EngagementManager` + `EngagementManagerId`. Seeded EM employees: Riya Kapoor, Rahul Sharma, Pradeep Singh, Arjun Mehta.
- Serilog file blocks: `Time : dd-MM-yyyy HH:mm:ss | PMS_DEBUG` (or `PMS_ERROR`) and `Message : ...`, wrapped in `===` lines.
- Resource Pool table columns sort like Directory (click header for A→Z / Z→A). Sortable: Dept, Emp Name, Reporting Manager, Allocation Status, Location, Office Site, Project Site. Allocation Type / Duration / Tasks stay plain headers.
- Resource Directory/Pool always opens on Directory after a first load or hard refresh. Pool stays in memory until you leave or reload; it is no longer kept in `?tab=`.
- Email inputs strip `# $ % ^ & *` and similar as you type. Allowed: letters, digits, `.` `_` `-`, and one `@`.
- Forms disable browser autofill (`autoComplete="off"`); email fields use text + `inputMode="email"` so Google/Chrome history suggestions do not appear while typing.
- Directory & Pool filters load departments from `mst_departments` and designations from `mst_designations` (not hardcoded frontend lists). Status filter is Active / Probation / Notice Period only.
- Onboard New Employee now sends the full profile payload (gender, DOB, address, emergency contact, marital status, nationality, dept/designation IDs, org + employment + skills fields). Those columns were empty because most form inputs were uncontrolled and `handleCreate` only POSTed a small subset.
- Profile reads the same API fields; probation row uses `ProbationStatus` with fallback to `ProbationPeriod`. Skills/certs/languages are comma-split lists.
- Integration test: `CreateEmployee_PersistsOnboardProfileFields`.
- Date of joining on onboard (and the profile date picker) is today or future only. API create rejects past joining dates. Existing employees keep historical dates on save.
- Toasts appear top-right: success = green + tick, error = red + alert icon.
- Customer details: SPOC Contacts stay empty until a sub-venture is selected; then that sub-venture's SPOCs are shown.
- Restored real dummy departments (Engineering, Product, Design, …). Tests no longer insert `Catalog Dept {guid}` rows.

